:CovetedFalcon rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Coveted Falcon" ;
    :manaCost "{1}{U}{U}" ;
    :manaValue "3"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Artifact ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Bird ;
    :hasRarity :Rare ;
    :hasColor :Blue ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Blue ;
    :isInSet :MurdersAtKarlovManor ;
    :cardNumber "48"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Madeline Boni" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "1" ;
    :powerValue "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "4" ;
    :toughnessValue "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Flying ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Disguise ;
    :printedText """Flying
Whenever this creature attacks, gain control of target permanent you own but don't control.
Disguise {1}{U}
When this creature is turned face up, target opponent gains control of any number of target permanents you control. Draw a card for each one they gained control of this way."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Flying
Whenever this creature attacks, gain control of target permanent you own but don't control.
Disguise {1}{U}
When this creature is turned face up, target opponent gains control of any number of target permanents you control. Draw a card for each one they gained control of this way."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=646610"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/48/coveted-falcon"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Turning a permanent face up or face down doesn't change whether that permanent is tapped or untapped."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A token's owner is the player who created it."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The face-down spell has no mana cost and a mana value of 0. When you cast a face-down spell, put it on the stack face down so no other player knows what it is, and pay {3} to cast it. This is an alternative cost."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A permanent that turns face up or face down changes characteristics but is otherwise the same permanent. Spells and abilities that were targeting that permanent and Auras and Equipment that were attached to that permanent aren't affected unless the new characteristics of the object change the legality of those targets or attachments."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Any time you have priority, you may turn the face-down creature face up by revealing what its disguise cost is and paying that cost. This is a special action. It doesn't use the stack and can't be responded to. Only a face-down permanent can be turned face up this way; a face-down spell cannot."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a face-down spell leaves the stack and goes to any zone other than the battlefield (if it was countered, for example), you must reveal it. Similarly, if a face-down permanent leaves the battlefield, you must reveal it. You must also reveal all face-down spells and permanents you control if you leave the game or the game ends."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You must ensure that your face-down spells and permanents can be easily differentiated from each other. You're not allowed to mix up the cards that represent them on the battlefield to confuse other players. The order in which they entered the battlefield should remain clear, as well as what ability caused them to be face down. (This includes disguise, cloak, and in games involving older cards, morph and manifest, as well as a few other effects that turn cards face down.) Common methods for doing this include using markers or dice, or simply placing them in order on the battlefield."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a face-down creature loses its abilities, it can't be turned face up with a disguise ability because it will no longer have a disguise ability (or a disguise cost) once face up."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Because face-down creatures don't have a name, they can't have the same name as any other creature, even another face-down creature."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """At any time, you can look at a face-down spell or permanent you control. You can't look at face-down permanents or spells you don't control unless an effect instructs or allows you to do so."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A disguise ability lets you cast a card face down by paying {3} and announcing that you are using a disguise ability. Any time you have priority, you can turn a face-down permanent with disguise face up by paying its disguise cost."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Because the permanent is on the battlefield both before and after it's turned face up, turning a permanent face up doesn't cause any enters-the-battlefield abilities to trigger."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The creature spell is a 2/2 creature spell with ward {2} that has no name, mana cost, or creature types. The resulting creature is a 2/2 creature with ward {2} that has no name, mana cost, or creature types. Both the spell and the resulting creature are colorless and have a mana value of 0. Other effects that apply to the spell or creature can still grant it any characteristics it doesn't have or change the characteristics it does have."""@en ] .

:KayaSpiritsJustice rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Kaya, Spirits' Justice" ;
    :manaCost "{2}{W}{B}" ;
    :manaValue "4"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasSuperType :Legendary ;
    :hasCardType :Planeswalker ;
    :hasSubType :Kaya ;
    :hasRarity :MythicRare ;
    :hasColor :White ;
    :hasColor :Black ;
    :hasColorIdentity :White ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Black ;
    :isInSet :MurdersAtKarlovManor ;
    :cardNumber "335"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Fay Dalton" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :loyalty "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAction :Surveil ;
    :printedText """Whenever one or more creatures you control and/or creature cards in your graveyard are put into exile, you may choose a creature card from among them. Until end of turn, target token you control becomes a copy of it, except it has flying.
+2: Surveil 2, then exile a card from a graveyard.
+1: Create a 1/1 white and black Spirit creature token with flying.
−2: Exile target creature you control. For each other player, exile up to one target creature that player controls."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Whenever one or more creatures you control and/or creature cards in your graveyard are put into exile, you may choose a creature card from among them. Until end of turn, target token you control becomes a copy of it, except it has flying.
+2: Surveil 2, then exile a card from a graveyard.
+1: Create a 1/1 white and black Spirit creature token with flying.
−2: Exile target creature you control. For each other player, exile up to one target creature that player controls."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=649712"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/335/kaya-spirits-justice"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a creature card that was exiled is no longer in exile when Kaya, Spirits' Justice's first ability resolves (perhaps because of Pull from Eternity or a similar effect), you can't choose that creature card with that ability."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You choose all targets for Kaya, Spirits' Justice's last ability."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-02-02"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The target token copies the printed values of the card in exile, with the noted exception. It doesn't matter if that card was a copy of something else when it was on the battlefield."""@en ] .
